 "capsule": "Unified as a single realm under Æthelstan, who was acclaimed king of the English in 927 and secured the union by crushing a Scottish-Viking coalition at the Battle of Brunanburh in 937, the Kingdom of England (Old English: Engla land) endured through Anglo-Saxon, Danish, Norman, Plantagenet, Tudor, and Stuart dynasties. It absorbed Wales under the Statute of Rhuddlan in 1284, and following the 1603 union of crowns with Scotland it was merged into the Kingdom of Great Britain by the Acts of Union of 1707.",
